Subject: [PATCH] ir3: bound A504 barrier register residency

The A530-derived barrier budget permits an A504 workgroup to deadlock at
bar.g.l before any shared-memory reads. Assembly bisection on the Lenovo M10
isolates a 64-invocation threshold: 16 full footprints, or 15 full plus one
half, complete the barrier; 16 full plus one half faults.

Halve the existing A504 barrier budget so the allocator spills as needed.
Do not change API limits, synchronization semantics or other shader stages.
This is an empirical barrier-residency bound, not a claim that the GPU's
entire physical register file is half the currently configured size.

The unchanged KHR-GLES31.core.compute_shader.shared-max then passes, as do
all 195 dEQP compute cases and 37 supported Khronos compute cases (2 skip).
No clock, watchdog or expected-failure changes are involved.

--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_ra.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_ra.c
@@ -2751,6 +2751,14 @@
       (wave_pairs_per_wg * (double_threadsize ? 2 : 1));
    assert(vec4_regs_per_thread > 0);
 
+   /* A504 needs a tighter bound for simultaneous barrier residency.
+    * A 64-invocation workgroup runs with 16 full footprints or 15 full
+    * plus one half, but deadlocks with 16 full plus one half.
+    * Keep this bound local to barriers; it is not a global regfile size.
+    */
+   if (fd_dev_gpu_id(compiler->dev_id) == 504)
+      vec4_regs_per_thread /= 2;
+
    return vec4_regs_per_thread * 4 * 2;
 }
 
